      "writtenOn": "2025-07-24T02:01:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question! In this case, it means that the same block can be found more than 256 times within the image. It\u0027s almost always either a solid color block, or a block with highly-regular pattern that has self-overlapping properties (like a checkerboard pattern), so it\u0027s easy to match in many ways.\n\nIt\u0027s desirable to keep many of these duplicates in memory, because some of these blocks will result in more favorable \"motion vectors\" that are smaller to code symbols for. However, keeping too many duplicates (\u003e256) will just end up slow down search for virtually no gain during my testing.",
      "parentUuid": "09fd5ffa_57209bff",
      "revId": "22391fed536d74a47ee0effcd2636efcd2764f6b",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
